Consider the following synchronization solution for Producer-Consumer problem. Here, counter is a shared variable
initialized to 0, buffer is the shared memory region and increment and decrement operations take place atomically.

Consumer process
item nextConsumed;
while (1) {
    while (counter == 0);
    nextConsumed = buffer[out];
    out = (out + 1) % BUFFER_SIZE;
    counter--;
}
Producer process
item nextProduced;
while (1) {
    while (counter == BUFFER_SIZE);
    buffer[in] = nextProduced;
    in = (in + 1) % BUFFER_SIZE;
    counter++;
}


