Fetch_And_Add is an atomic Read-Modify-Write instruction that reads the value of memory location say X , and
increments it by the value say i, and returns the old value of X . It is used in the pseudocode shown below to implement a
ticket lock. yield() is a method that causes the current thread to give up execution to another thread that is ready to
run..A ticket lock is a synchronization mechanism that uses "tickets" to control which thread of execution is allowed to
enter a critical section. Initially, turn = ticket = 0

typedef struct {
    int ticket;
    int turn;
} lock_t;

void lock_init(lock_t *lock) {
    lock->ticket = 0;
    lock->turn = 0;
}

void acquire(lock_t *lock) {
    int myturn = Fetch_And_Add(&lock->ticket);
    while (lock->turn != myturn)
          yield();
}

void release(lock_t *lock) {
    lock->turn += 1;
}

Following is the implementation of Fetch_And_Add(FAA):

int FAA(int *ptr) {
    int old = *ptr;
    *ptr = old + 1;
    return old;
}

